#X text 240 83 the object performs run-length decoding: it expands
a list of single elements according to the corresponding repeat counts;
#X text 240 138 the first inlet receives the list of elements \, the
second inlet receives the list of repeat counts; the first element
is repeated as many times as the first count \, and so on;
#X text 240 208 the object can be used to restore a list compressed
by [list.rlencode] \, for example to decode a sequence of repeated
notes or values;
